&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-.25in'>A.&lt;span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span>Interpretation
of texts often comes in terms of the assumed overall viewpoints, more than by
the requirements of the text under discussion. Hence, we can’t solve the
problem itself because we are not dealing with the whole viewpoint that gives
credence to the idea on this text.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>INTERPRETATION, HERMENEUTICS, THEOLOGICAL METHOD</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/interpretation/interpretation-hermeneutics-theological-method/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/interpretation/interpretation-hermeneutics-theological-method/</guid><description>&lt;style>
