tranquility),&lt;/span>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:
"Times New Roman",serif'> spirit &lt;/span>&lt;span style='font-size:10.0pt;
line-height:115%;font-family:"Times New Roman",serif'>(&lt;i>vs&lt;/i>. physical
circumcision for naturalization into a physical nation)&lt;/span>&lt;span
style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:"Times New Roman",serif'>.
All the features of interpersonalism contrast with their opposites. The first
and second great commandments (cp. Golden Rule) deal with love, the
summarizing, most important, outward-directed pattern of interpersonal action,
which produces the other interpersonal actions. As Micah&lt;b> 6&lt;/b>:8 said of
old, &lt;i>“What does the Lord require of you but to do justly, love kindness, and
walk humbly with your God”&lt;/i> &lt;/span>&lt;span style='font-size:10.0pt;line-height:
115%;font-family:"Times New Roman",serif'>(&lt;/span>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt;
